00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.740
Mutsuko!

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.010
We lost.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.440
I'm home!

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:12.110
<b>Nice Game!</b>

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.360
Izumi!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.320
Pop? You're home?

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:19.520
Hm? Is that a bad thing?

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.390
All righty! Let's go play catch before dinner!

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:23.580
C'mon, let's play!

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.120
What? Are you serious?

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.000
I've got cram school, and I wanna shower—

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:28.720
Huh?!

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.600
So you're just giving up on these precious
fleeting moments of direct communication

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:35.050
we get as parent and child?!
Is this the "rebellious teens"?!

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:38.470
You didn't have to start bawling.

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:39.930
I'll play, but only for a bit.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:45.470
Sheesh. You play baseball all year round, yet
you still wanna play catch when you get home.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.490
It's like I said...

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:52.810
It's my way of communicating
with my precious daughter and son.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:55.530
Got ya!

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:55.870
Hey!

00:02:57.310 --> 00:02:59.300
The angle of the glove is
key when catching there.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.700
Tingles, doesn't it?

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:00.700
Oh, come on!

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.410
Hey, that reminds me.
It was Daigo's district final today.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.600
Do you know what the final score was?

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.120
I went and watched.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:13.080
They lost to a walk-off home run.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.540
Oh. I see.

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.010
But they put up a really good 
fight against a strong team.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:23.070
A lot's happened at Fuurin 
since you graduated.

00:03:23.070 --> 00:03:27.270
Without a coach, and in their first real
tournament, your successors did well.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:34.610
But this is just the start
of his baseball career.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.000
These baseball nuts...

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.280
And we're done.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.990
Izumi, please set the table.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.290
Coming.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.950
Wow, that looks amazing.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:48.550
I'm home.

00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:53.710
Welcome back!

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:55.140
You must be really hungry.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.260
Dinner's ready.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.150
I don't want any.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.510
I'm not hungry.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.850
He went on about this tourney being
a trial run, and now he's acting like that?

00:04:04.850 --> 00:04:06.510
He couldn't be more down if he tried.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:08.200
Well, it's only natural.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:10.770
They were so close to
winning the Districts, after all.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.480
<i>Ah, this is bad.</i>

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:22.400
<i>That hurt way too much.</i>

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.460
<i>This handwriting...</i>

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.520
<i>He came and saw my game?</i>

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.420
Pop...

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:44.300
Mom!

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:46.520
Hey, Mom!

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.470
Mom!

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.230
What is it?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:54.050
I just realized I'm actually starving.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:56.500
So I was wondering what was for dinner.

00:04:56.500 --> 00:04:59.150
Didn't you say you weren't hungry?

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.440
That's what I heard.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:02.550
Oh, I was just a little...

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:07.410
You're really not gonna let me eat?!

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.450
Of course I will.

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:10.620
Don't start crying.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.560
Look!

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:13.580
Wow!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.810
Tonight, it's hamburg
steak in a demi-glace sauce!

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.810
I even added Pop's portion 
to yours, so it's humongous!

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:20.210
No kidding!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.730
Wait, so he left already?

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:22.810
Yeah...

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:26.300
He never changes. By now, he should
already be in the air on his way to Kochi.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:27.580
Oh, right.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:29.930
He just jumped up all of
a sudden and said he was off.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:33.540
When I asked him about dinner,
he told me to give you his portion.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:35.230
Ah, so that's why.

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:38.280
You don't have to eat it all.
Don't make yourself sick.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.260
Right.

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:41.110
Let's eat!

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.450
<i>Give it your all, Daigo.</i>

