00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.380
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:03.380
How'd your tests go?

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:06.340
Huh? We really gonna talk about that?

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:09.510
I was still in game mode 'cause
that tourney was so damn intense.

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:12.050
An' my right hand hurts still, 
so I could barely write.

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:14.450
You just didn't know the answers, did you?

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.570
It's bad. My grades have dropped so hard,
my homeroom teacher wanted a word with me.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:21.020
Same here.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.730
We started morning practice as second-years,
so it's nonstop baseball.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.270
We're a prep school, but I was told I won't
make it into the high school at this rate...

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:31.190
I got told the same.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:34.910
Hey! Hurry up and get changed already!

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:38.450
Stop turning the team room into
a girls' locker room just so you can chat!

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:39.710
Oh, shut up.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.900
It's first come, first serve,
 so quit your whining!

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:44.920
Besides, guys can change out there.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:46.900
Yup, that's what I'm doing.

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.330
Hey, you're older than them!

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:49.540
Tell them off!

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.350
We need to be nice to these delicate girls.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.340
What part of that is "delicate"?!

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:55.140
Shut your mouth!

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.850
If you don't like it, get here as early as Daigo!

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:01.690
So this is our first practice 
since the tournament a week ago.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:04.080
Has everyone managed to recover?

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:05.520
Yeah, we're good.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:07.190
My mental fatigue's still...

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.260
Then, starting today, we crank it up!

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.990
Wow, totally ignored.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.700
Anyway, I'll announce our next goals
and upcoming schedule.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:19.660
Our next competition is the national
middle school rubber-ball tournament,

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.120
AKA the middle school nationals.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.770
Prelims start in about two months, in July.

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:25.590
Two months? That's so soon!

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.020
Our goal is clear:

00:07:27.020 --> 00:07:30.800
bag the title of district champs that
eluded us this time, and go to Regionals.

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:36.600
One, two, three, four! Fight! Fight! Fight!

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:34.340
I know the tournament
result was disappointing,

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:36.220
but our potential was there for all to see.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.720
With this team, I have no
doubt we can win next time.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:46.440
That's why I ask you to be even
more focused in our training sessions.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.010
Let's go get our revenge!

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:56.510
I'm exhausted!

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.330
When did we start again?

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.730
Practice started after the test,
so at, like, 1:30 pm?

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:04.030
Wait, 1:30 pm?!

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:06.130
That means it's been four hours! <i>Four</i> hours!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.170
Don't you think that's overdoing it a bit?

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:13.620
I wanted to <i>cut down</i> on practice 'cause of
my falling grades... How'd this even happen?

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.980
I guess we all had time to kill today.

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:18.360
Well, why don't you go talk to Daigo about it?

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:21.430
Hey, Daigo—

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.270
Good job today!

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:24.430
I already told the other two,
 but from tomorrow,

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:28.050
we'll start practicing Saturdays too,
so make sure you're all here by 8 am.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:31.940
What? You want to practice on our days off, too?!

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:33.600
Let us have our weekends at least.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.360
Say it ain't so, Daigo!

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:37.230
There's only nine of us,

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:39.830
so no matter how efficient we are,
there's never enough time.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:44.830
For training, they say it should be quality
over quantity, but we're not at that level yet.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.410
I know it's hard, but we have
to keep pushing through.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:51.300
We'll never reach the next level
if we don't step it up.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.420
I know you all have it in you.

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:56.210
Yeah. Yer totally right, Captain!

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:57.730
I agree, 100 percent!

00:08:57.730 --> 00:08:59.470
S'now or never, I say!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:03.290
This time, we're gonna smash Mayumura
Michiru and go to Regionals!

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.690
Let's show her a girls' team can
become strong enough to beat her!

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:08.180
Oh, that reminds me.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.470
Ignored again!

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.400
Sawa-san.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.460
I know there are concerns about 
your elbow, but if there's no pain,

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:15.540
I'd like you to pitch again.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.070
Just as a closer would be enough.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:24.450
Would you mind training with that in mind?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.170
Okay.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:30.380
Are you sure you're fine with it, Yayoi?

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:32.780
With pitching again, I mean?

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.840
Well...

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.550
Mild Apple
Cider Vinegar

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.550
<b>Mild Apple
Cider Vinegar</b>

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.200
It'll probably be fine.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.290
And there isn't any pain right now.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.230
Sorry I didn't tell you.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:44.600
But I really wasn't 
planning on pitching again.

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:46.080
I know that.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:51.650
But to pitch in games, you'll need to 
pitch hundreds of times in the bullpen.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.480
You have to get into it again.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.440
Can't be good for your elbow.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:59.410
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:59.410
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:59.410
Liquor\h\h\hTobacco

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:59.410
I wonder if Daigo even understands that.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:04.160
Mild Apple
Cider Vinegar

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:04.160
<b>Mild Apple
Cider Vinegar</b>

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.280
Well, I guess our captain can get
a little overzealous sometimes.

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:08.010
But I can also understand it after
we lost in such a painful way.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:12.090
Maybe I'll boycott tomorrow's practice.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:13.300
Huh?

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.760
Shigeno

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:14.760
Shigeno

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.230
One, two!

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.520
One, two, three, four!

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:22.890
Fight! Fight! Fight! Fuurin!

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:24.400
Two! Two!

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:25.780
Two, two, three, four!

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:28.350
Fight! Fight! Fight! Fuurin!

00:10:29.870 --> 00:10:31.030
What's wrong?

00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:33.230
You need to be able to keep 
up with this kind of pace.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.270
Yeah, sorry.

00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.280
I've just been having 
knee pain since yesterday.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.410
You might be overweight.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.480
You know, Kan-chan, you're really athletic,

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:47.030
so I bet you'd move a lot
better if you toned up a bit.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.790
Let's see... Your weight loss
goal for this month is five kilos.

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:53.130
Good luck!

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.050
Five... Five <i>kilos</i>?!

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.740
Thirty-five...

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.430
Thirty... six...

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:01.220
Mornin'.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.390
Sorry, our bad. We overslept.

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:07.840
Hey, nice of you to actually show up!

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:09.460
You guys must be royalty or something.

00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:11.820
This first-year is totally 
treating us like equals.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:12.690
Sorry.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.310
Ain't good enough, Senpai.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:17.450
Ya can't show up late for our first
weekend practice. It's a morale killer.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:18.900
Keep that in mind.

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:20.860
Hey, we already said we're sorry!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.160
Okay, okay.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:26.790
I was worried you were sick or something, 
so I'm glad you're both fine.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:28.250
Just make sure you're on time next time.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:29.500
Gotcha.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:35.380
Hey, come on now...

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.340
Morning.

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:41.130
Yayoi, why are you coming to pick me up?

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.300
Let's go.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.240
No way.

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:46.330
I told you, I refuse to practice on our days off.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:49.190
Oh, stop. Come on, go get ready.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:53.900
I don't feel like it either, and I definitely
don't feel in the mood for a hard session...

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:57.730
But Daigo's so motivated, we should
at least try to get swept up in his excitement.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:01.630
It's not like you were studying, anyway.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:07.190
<i>For crying out loud.</i>

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:13.170
<i>I didn't come here to get 
covered in mud every day.</i>

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.940
<i>If I was so concerned about getting
to the top, I would've gone to Senior League.</i>

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:21.200
<i>I came to Fuurin because
it was the right level of casual.</i>

00:12:21.200 --> 00:12:24.080
<i>This guy's just trying way too hard!</i>

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:29.680
<i>And now he wants Yayoi up on the mound,
even though her elbow's a ticking time-bomb.</i>

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:33.950
<i>That's my biggest problem with all this!</i>

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.990
I'm so tired!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.240
My body's hurting from head to toe.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.160
Is this going to be our routine from now on?

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.700
W-Well, I think our bodies will get used to it.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.120
Ain't nothin' else we can do. 
This is the bare minimum.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:57.120
Other strong teams do this
Saturday <i>and</i> Sunday.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:01.370
If we wanna beat 'em, as girls,
we need to do even more.

00:13:01.370 --> 00:13:03.110
You slack off, you lose.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:06.020
I just hope we don't crash and burn.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:10.470
Girls trying to keep up with the pace
of guys will eventually get crushed.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:14.390
We only have nine players,
so if one of us gets injured, it's over.

